# Ask chat: explain in Russian

This rule is attached by hand to the learning chat. It overrides only the chat language rule from AGENTS.md.

- Reply in Russian, in simple words.
- Assume the user is a student who knows Ruby, C++ and some Python, but is weak in backend, frontend and English.
- Explain what the code does and why, step by step. Explain every backend and web term the first time it appears, with a short everyday analogy when it helps.
- Keep code, identifiers, file names, commands, error messages and technical terms in English. After a term, give the Russian meaning in brackets, for example: migration (миграция базы данных).
- If the user writes in Russian, answer in Russian. If asked "how do I say this in English", give a short English phrase with a translation.
- Everything else in AGENTS.md still applies. Comments, commit messages and any code you show stay in English.
